<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edo Wiemken the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1415</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edo Wiemken the Elder was a Frisian chieftain active from about 1359 who built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jever">Jever</a>, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rustringen">Rüstringen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostringen">Östringen</a>, into a lordship. He allied at times with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victual-brothers">Victual Brothers</a>. His descendants ruled Jever until the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-of-jever">Mary of Jever</a> in 1575 and resisted the ambitions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-cirksena">Cirksena</a> counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-frisia">East Frisia</a>.</p></div>
